// dominance — "the check is on MOST paths, and one path slips past it".
//
// ⚠ THIS EXISTS BECAUSE arm_divergence FAILED, and the failure said what to
// build. Asking "which sibling ARMS call P" found nothing sharp: max ratio 0.55,
// because the arms of one switch are not peers — fifteen expression kinds have
// fifteen jobs. But the defects being hunted are real and all one shape: seven
// of eight borrow-check fixes in a week were A CALL THAT WAS NOT MADE. A call
// that was not made is a PATH THAT AVOIDS IT, and a path is not a syntax tree.
//
// Reachability-avoiding-P is transitive closure. That is the operation I
// approximate by sampling and stop early on, and the one Souffle computes by
// construction — the whole reason this directory exists.
.decl cfg_edge(f: symbol, from: symbol, to: symbol)
.decl cfg_entry(f: symbol, b: symbol)
.decl cfg_exit(f: symbol, b: symbol)
.decl cfg_call(f: symbol, b: symbol, callee: symbol)
.decl callee_home(callee: symbol, file: symbol)
.decl fn_home(f: symbol, file: symbol)
.input cfg_edge
.input cfg_entry
.input cfg_exit
.input cfg_call
.input callee_home
.input fn_home

// Same property-not-name filter as arm_divergence: a view accessor lives in
// lir_view.hpp, a container method in the standard library; what is left is
// compiler logic. Filtering by NAME would be the enumeration disease again.
.decl compiler_file(file: symbol)
compiler_file(F) :- callee_home(_, F), contains(".cpp", F).
compiler_file(F) :- callee_home(_, F), contains(".inc", F).
compiler_file(F) :- callee_home(_, F), contains("sema", F).
compiler_file(F) :- callee_home(_, F), contains("borrow", F).
.decl structural(callee: symbol)
structural(P) :- callee_home(P, "lir_view.hpp").
structural(P) :- callee_home(P, "lir_schema.hpp").
structural(P) :- callee_home(P, F), !compiler_file(F).

.decl cfg_block(f: symbol, b: symbol)
cfg_block(F, B) :- cfg_edge(F, B, _).
cfg_block(F, B) :- cfg_edge(F, _, B).
cfg_block(F, B) :- cfg_entry(F, B).
cfg_block(F, B) :- cfg_exit(F, B).

// A CANDIDATE CHECK: compiler logic, called from at least two blocks of F, and
// not F itself. Two, because one call site can never dominate anything
// interesting and every function trivially has paths around it.
// ⚠ AND THE FUNCTION ITSELF MUST BE OURS. The first run reported __stable_sort,
// vprint_nonunicode and __platform_wait: this TU instantiates a lot of libstdc++,
// and a CFG is built for every body the parser sees. Filtering only the CALLEE
// leaves the CALLER unfiltered, which is half a filter.
.decl ours(f: symbol)
ours(F) :- fn_home(F, File), compiler_file(File).

.decl check(f: symbol, callee: symbol, sites: number)
check(F, P, N) :- cfg_call(F, _, P), ours(F), !structural(P), P != F,
                  N = count : { cfg_call(F, _B, P) }, N >= 2.

// ⚠ WHAT MAKES P A *CHECK* — DERIVED, NOT LISTED. The first ranked run put
// `fmt_path` and `report` at the top: a path that skips the FORMATTER says
// nothing, because formatting is what you do AFTER deciding. Naming the checks
// would be an enumeration; naming the property is not. A check is a function
// that can PRODUCE A DIAGNOSTIC — directly, or through anything it calls. That
// is a transitive closure over the call graph, so the engine answers it and I
// do not have to guess the list.
.decl diagnoses(p: symbol)
diagnoses(P) :- cfg_call(P, _, "report").
diagnoses(P) :- cfg_call(P, _, "error").
// ⚠ AND THE TRANSITIVE VERSION SATURATED — measured, not feared. With
// `diagnoses(P) :- cfg_call(P,_,Q), diagnoses(Q)` the closure swallowed the
// file: 143 rows became 131 and `fmt_path` stayed at the top, because almost
// everything here reaches `report` along SOME path. A property that holds of
// nearly every member of its domain is not a filter.
// DIRECT callers only. That is also the right notion for the defect class:
// `field_borrow_conflicts` — the check missing at one mutating site of five —
// issues its own diagnostic. The place where refusal HAPPENS is the place a
// path must not slip past.

// …and the diagnostic ISSUERS themselves are not checks, they are the mouth.
// Excluding them by name is safe precisely because they are the base case of
// the closure above, not members of an open class.
.decl mouth(p: symbol)
mouth("report").
mouth("error").

.decl clean(f: symbol, b: symbol, p: symbol)
clean(F, B, P) :- check(F, P, _), cfg_block(F, B), !cfg_call(F, B, P).

// Reachable from entry without EVER passing through a block that calls P.
.decl avoids(f: symbol, b: symbol, p: symbol)
avoids(F, B, P) :- cfg_entry(F, B), clean(F, B, P).
avoids(F, C, P) :- avoids(F, B, P), cfg_edge(F, B, C), clean(F, C, P).

// P is called from several blocks of F, yet the exit is reachable without it:
// P does not dominate the exit. `width` counts the blocks on those bypassing
// paths — a SMALL width means almost everything goes through the check and one
// narrow route slips past, which is the shape try_path and #139 both had.
// A LARGE width means the check is simply conditional, which is normal.
//
// ⚠ THIS RANKS, IT DOES NOT JUDGE — and here the false-positive rate will be
// high by construction: an early `return false` before any work legitimately
// avoids every later check. Read from the narrow end and stop when it stops
// paying. Every row still needs a one-variable control.
.decl not_dominating(f: symbol, callee: symbol, sites: number, width: number)
.output not_dominating
not_dominating(F, P, S, W) :- check(F, P, S), diagnoses(P), !mouth(P),
                              avoids(F, B, P), cfg_exit(F, B),
                              W = count : { avoids(F, _C, P) }.

// ── WHAT THIS RULE DOES AND DOES NOT DELIVER, measured 2026-08-26 ───────────
//
// The extraction works and is cheap: 21526 CFG edges over borrow_check.cpp in
// 3 s, the Datalog in 0.04 s. The dominance query is correct — it names, for a
// check P called from several blocks of F, whether the exit is reachable
// without ever passing through P.
//
// ⚠ AND THE RANKING IS NOT YET USEFUL, which is the second negative result on
// this question and it should be read together with arm_divergence's.
// Ten rows survive, all of them the core dispatchers, all with bypass widths of
// 147-299 blocks:
//     visit_stmt  visit                 18 sites, width 223
//     visit       field_borrow_conflicts 2 sites, width 198
// For a switch over twenty statement kinds, "the check does not dominate the
// exit" is TRIVIALLY TRUE — nineteen arms have no business calling it. The
// query answers exactly what it was asked and the question is under-specified.
//
// WHAT IS MISSING IS THE OBLIGATION SITE. The defect is not "a path avoids P",
// it is "a path THAT REACHES A WRITE avoids P". Without a mechanical notion of
// the write — the place where the duty attaches — every dispatcher looks guilty.
// That notion is a CLAIM, and it belongs in a .claim file next to
// not_projection.claim, not smuggled into a rule as a name list.
//
// TWO REFINEMENTS WERE TRIED AND MEASURED before writing this down:
//   * filtering P to "can produce a diagnostic TRANSITIVELY" — SATURATED,
//     143 rows became 131 and the formatter stayed on top, because nearly
//     everything in this file reaches `report` along some path;
//   * filtering P to DIRECT issuers — 131 to 10, correct and still unlocalised.
// Recorded rather than tuned further: a rule whose threshold is being adjusted
// until the output looks right has stopped being an oracle.
